INT. HOUSEBOAT SALON - CANAL AMSTERDAM - NIGHT

A narrow wooden cabin crammed with antique clocks. A potbellied stove. A low table with a half-eaten cheese board. Rain drums on the roof. Candles. Six people, one body in the corner under a tablecloth.

INSPECTOR LEOPOLD VAN DER MEULEN-OSEI (50s, pipe, a fold of paper in his pocket) paces the length of the room. At the stove, MADAME CATHERINE ABERNATHY-DUPRE (60s, rings, silk robe) warms her hands. On the sofa, TOBIAS "TOBY" NGUYEN-HARTMANN (30s, in his socks, a glass of whiskey). Beside him, CLEMENTINE ODUYA-BRANDT (20s, long braids, a shoebox on her knees). In the armchair, BRUNO ADELEKE-FISCHER (50s, a sleeping cap pushed back). At the window, SISTER IMOGEN FAIRBANKS-TEMBO (40s, habit, rosary).

LEOPOLD
Ladies and gentlemen, I would like silence.

TOBY
You've had silence for an hour.

BRUNO
You've had it and you've done nothing with it.

LEOPOLD
I have been thinking.

CATHERINE
We could hear you thinking. You hum.

LEOPOLD
(to the room)
Everyone, please, remain where you are.

CLEMENTINE
Why would anyone move?

IMOGEN
There is a body, child.

CLEMENTINE
I know there's a body, Sister.

TOBY
Can we talk about the body?

BRUNO
No.

CATHERINE
Yes.

LEOPOLD
Madame Abernathy-Dupre, you found him.

CATHERINE
I did.

LEOPOLD
And you screamed.

CATHERINE
Of course I screamed.

LEOPOLD
Mr. Ngu-- Mr. Nguyen-Hartmann, you ran in first.

TOBY
I was in the kitchen.

BRUNO
You were in the hallway.

TOBY
I was walking through the hallway to the kitchen.

CLEMENTINE
He had his shoes on.

TOBY
So?

CLEMENTINE
Now he's in his socks.

Silence. The stove ticks. A clock chimes, then another, a few seconds out of step.

LEOPOLD
Mr. Nguyen-Hartmann, where are your shoes?

TOBY
(low)
By the door.

LEOPOLD
Then why did you take them off?

TOBY
Because they were wet.

IMOGEN
Wet from what?

TOBY
The deck. Rain.

CATHERINE
(to herself)
The deck. The deck. Of course.

LEOPOLD
Sister Imogen, you were at the window.

IMOGEN
I was praying.

LEOPOLD
For how long?

IMOGEN
Until I heard the scream.

LEOPOLD
And what did you see?

IMOGEN
The canal.

BRUNO
There's nothing to see on the canal at night.

IMOGEN
There was a boat.

LEOPOLD
What boat?

IMOGEN
A small one. With one oar.

The clocks chime again, all together, a ragged, solemn chord. Clementine opens her shoebox, lifts out a single wet shoe. Everyone stares at it.

CLEMENTINE
It was on the deck. I found it.

TOBY
That's not mine.

CLEMENTINE
It's a man's. Size eleven.

BRUNO
(sitting up)
That's mine.

LEOPOLD
Mr. Adeleke-Fischer.

BRUNO
It's mine. I lost it last week.

LEOPOLD
You said you were asleep.

BRUNO
I was asleep.

LEOPOLD
In one shoe.

BRUNO
It's a very old habit.

Nobody laughs. The rain slows.

LEOPOLD
Everyone, please, stay calm.

CATHERINE
(quietly)
I am very calm.

She picks up the poker from the stove and holds it loosely, like a conductor's baton.

LEOPOLD
Madame, put that down.

CATHERINE
Of course.

She doesn't.
